  "notes": "めらめら vividly describes actively burning flames, and is often used metaphorically for intense emotions.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ぼうぼう: burning/blazing (large fire)\n- ちろちろ: flickering weakly\n- ごうごう: roaring (large fire)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- めらめら{燃|も}える: to blaze, to burn fiercely\n- めらめらと{燃|も}え{上|あ}がる: to flare up",
